  "author_notes": "Records cover every quarter in the B.M. program with an ensemble and a lesson, so 'every quarter' and the 9/6 minimums both hold in pass records. MUSC 31 is taken in all three MUSC 30 quarters (the note's failed-section exception is not exercised). MUSC 196B is treated as the lesson for its quarter (the page says it replaces applied lessons). Ambiguities: the exact quarter a student enters the B.M. program is not in the record (the late-start pass case only omits the first fall quarter, before any B.M. audition could occur); the two-ensembles-in-one-quarter fail case necessarily leaves a lesson quarter without a concurrent ensemble, which is the same ensemble deficiency. Attestation names used: 'B.M. audition', 'continuing B.M. juries', 'senior recital'. AUDIT: removed fail-transfer-two-ensembles-one-quarter as ambiguous/multi: the quarter left without an ensemble still has a MUSC 161 lesson, which violates the lessons section's 'Concurrent enrollment in an appropriate ensemble is required', so whether one or two requirements fail depends on reading that sentence as a degree rule; the one-ensemble-per-quarter cap cannot be isolated because any missed ensemble quarter also breaks the parallel lessons rule.",
